########## # Solution ##########
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION To solve for [`y\text{,}`] we first isolate [`5y`] by subtracting [`2x`] from each side of the equation. After that, we can divide each side by [`5`] to finish solving for [`y\text{:}`]
[``` \begin{aligned} 2x+5\attention{y}\amp=10\\ 2x+5\attention{y}\subtractright{2x}\amp=10\subtractright{2x}\\ 5\attention{y}\amp=10-2x\\ \divideunder{5\attention{y}}{5}\amp=\divideunder{10-2x}{5}\\ y\amp=\frac{10-2x}{5} \end{aligned} ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
############# # End Problem #############
